"""Session 6. Build 1: a no-code workflow. Build clock: 10 recall and setup, 20 idea, 15 demonstration, 5 break, 60 learner (5 plan, 30 build, 25 test), 10 test log and decision.

The Zap follows the Zapier Build Guide: six parts in this order: trigger, AI step, human approval, filter, log, notify. The Filter is required and runs after
the approval. Learners make a copy of the instructor-prepared sheet 'Zapier Practice'. Screens change, so no slide describes a screen layout as fact; the
instructor tries every step in a real account first. No AI output is shown as observed.
"""

